      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The fine dust near stems could suggest spider mites, which are very small and notoriously hard to spot without magnification. These microscopic pests suck sap, causing stippling and sometimes lodging small holes if they are heavily infested. Another possibility is thrips, which can also leave tiny feeding marks and may appear as a fine residue when active. Consider checking the stems and new growth more frequently and using a strong jet of water to dislodge them.",
